      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. That is about twice the FDA-labeled maximum of 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin. Most guidelines recommend staying at or below 2,000\u20132,550 mg/day. Doses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, and they give no added glycemic benefit.\n\nHere are some possible explanations:\n- **Typo or unit error.** For example, 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg/day) or 500 mg three times daily may have been intended.\n- **Total daily dose entered as a single dose.** For example, 1,700 mg/day split into smaller doses, such as 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Wrong drug or formulation.** Check this if the order was meant to be something else.\n\nPlease check the intended dose with your resident or attending. Once you have the corrected dose, I can enter it right away. Typical options are:\n- **Starting dose:** 500 mg by mouth twice daily with meals, or 850 mg once daily.\n- **Common maintenance dose:** 850 mg by mouth twice or three times daily with meals. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day.\n\nWhat dose would you like me to enter?"
      }
     ],
